1
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:12,860
My son, my precious boy has been murdered!

2
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,980
I can sense the misfortune
that has befallen my son.

3
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,120
The bond between mother
and son has spoken!

4
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:46,000
My precious, beautiful boy, you
died covered with wounds like this!

5
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,200
Those bastards!

6
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,580
I can feel it!

7
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,080
I suffer the same pain you felt!

8
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:59,440
You were utterly magnificent as you
fought for Lord Dio, my dear centerfold!

9
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,130
How?

10
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:06,300
How did they do it to kill such
a noble and pure soul like you?

11
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:11,220
They must have done something underhanded!

12
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,040
Stop them!

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,830
The bastards!

14
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:23,917
I will make sure they pay a terrifying
price with the Empress card!

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,300
They'll regret the day they were born!

16
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,070
Move!

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,640
I won't stand idle!

18
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,540
This is the time for action!

19
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:37,680
A time for vengeance with a
stand that brings a slow death!

20
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,120
The anguish, the pain!

21
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:48,960
I shall kill them all!

22
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:11,320
Thank you.

23
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:47,257
Thank

24
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,657
you

25
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:55,740
so

26
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:00,810
much for watching.

27
00:03:00,893 --> 00:03:02,800
You're the one who's going to die.

28
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,297
The one who's going to die.

29
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:06,897
We're the one who's going to die.

30
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:07,810
JoJo!

31
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:31,140
JoJo and crew, head to
the sacred city Varanasi.

32
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:33,580
Listen up.

33
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:38,960
I don't usually get on a soapbox like
this, but stupid people are just that.

34
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:42,777
You could repeat something a million
times over and they still won't listen.

35
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:44,297
You know the type, don't you?

36
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:46,577
There's just no helping the poor souls.

37
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:48,880
But you know, uh, hold on.

38
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,100
I never got your name, did I?

39
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,050
Nena.

40
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:54,709
Nena, that's a great name.

41
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:58,817
Daughter of a wealthy family in the sacred
city Varanasi that we're passing through,

42
00:03:58,900 --> 00:03:59,730
right?

43
00:03:59,813 --> 00:04:03,257
You're good looking, and you've got an
equally good head on your shoulders.

44
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:06,760
I have an eye for people,
which leads me to my point.

45
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:10,940
Hole Horse is a horrible
lying bastard, understand?

46
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:12,900
He was manipulating you.

47
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,180
Think how your parents would feel.

48
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,500
You hear me?

49
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,817
You can't end up like this, okay?

50
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,017
I know it's easy when you're in love,

51
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:24,457
but you can't afford to see the
world with such a narrow view.

52
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:27,117
Take a step back and look
at the whole picture.

53
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,720
Hey, we're almost there.

54
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:33,260
The city of Varanasi.

55
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:39,060
The sacred river, the Ganges.

56
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,220
A place for holy men,

57
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:46,797
the old and the sick, where domestic
animals and food for human consumption?

58
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:50,980
lie alongside human waste
and corpses for cremation.

59
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:54,680
The river embraces all.

60
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:01,600
From birth unto death, its holy
waters form a microcosm of life.

61
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:08,060
It is said that visitors of the sacred
city of Varanasi remain transfixed,

62
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:09,813
never wanting to leave.

63
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:16,020
Perhaps the landscape that is this
sacred land is a mirror unto the soul.

64
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,110
Hmm?

65
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:33,760
Man, this thing isn't getting any better.

66
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,134
What's wrong, old man?

67
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,576
You don't look well.

68
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,050
Uh-uh.

69
00:05:43,133 --> 00:05:45,588
Looks like my bug bite
just got a lot worse.

70
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,447
This thing must be infected.

71
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,160
It's definitely swollen.

72
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:52,437
It would be best to have a doctor
look at it before it gets worse.

73
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:56,200
Hey, doesn't that sort of
look like a person's face?

74
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,557
Stop kidding around, Polnareff.

75
00:05:58,640 --> 00:05:59,470
That's creepy.

76
00:06:00,020 --> 00:06:01,160
Sorry about that.

77
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,177
Want me to go to the hospital with you?

78
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,090
No!

79
00:06:04,173 --> 00:06:05,781
Stop treating me like an old man.

80
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,390
Hmm.

81
00:06:12,473 --> 00:06:14,580
I'll just lance this. Huh?

82
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:15,900
What did you say?

83
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,880
It's definitely infected now.

84
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,317
It'll get worse if we
don't drain the fluid.

85
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:25,320
Hey, hey, hey, can't we just put medicine
and a bandage on it and call it a day?

86
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,953
Don't worry, my friend.

87
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,376
We'll numb the area so it won't hurt.

88
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,380
No problem.

89
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,000
No problem at all.

90
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,880
Come now, lie down.

91
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:40,357
Sir, I studied medicine in England.

92
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,420
I can do appendectomies, too.

93
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,760
Uh-oh, it's a little rusty.

94
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:46,980
Well, that's no problem.

95
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,400
All right, let's slice it open.

96
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,417
Come on, I don't want to
watch it being cut open.

97
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,340
Have a heart!

98
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,660
It'll be fine.

99
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,300
Hey, are you done yet?

100
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,140
Can I open my eyes now?

101
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,340
What the?

102
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,237
Hey, doctor!

103
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,920
Trying to cut me off?

104
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,220
That's a pretty stupid move, you old fart!

105
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:37,740
Choo-me-me!

106
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,210
What the...

107
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:40,480
what the hell is this?

108
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:41,960
I am the empress!

109
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:44,560
As in the empress part, old man Joseph!

110
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:47,600
And now, I'm gonna bloody you up blood!

111
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:51,740
When did you get on me, dammit?

112
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,740
No way, this thing's got teeth?

113
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,780
Damn thing's strong!

114
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,000
No, it grabbed the scalpel!

115
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,660
Oh, no!

116
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,609
Thank goodness that
was my artificial hand!

117
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,960
Bastard, think you can just cut me?

118
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:14,140
I'm a part of your body
now, old man Joseph!

119
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:18,420
You can't get away from me,
honey, no matter how hard you try.

120
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:23,217
You know, I bet I can tell you what's
going through that thick skull of yours.

121
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:27,829
You're probably thinking something like,
only a stand can beat another stand.

122
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:32,137
My stand, Hermit Purple, has the power
of clairvoyance and remote viewing.

123
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,677
But how am I supposed to fight
something like this with those powers?

124
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:39,760
How can I destroy something
that's growing out of my own arms?

125
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:42,580
So, honey, was that spot on?

126
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:44,077
Where's the user?

127
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,517
How in the hell could
you have infected me?

128
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,380
You moron! I won't tell!

129
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,360
Disgusting freak!

130
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,727
Running off to your friends?

131
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,940
We'll see how that goes, won't we?

132
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:02,880
Doctor, your next patient
is waiting for you.

133
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:08,390
Doctor!

134
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,060
Hey, don't get the wrong idea.

135
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,110
I didn't...

136
00:09:13,193 --> 00:09:14,940
I killed him! Hey!

137
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,320
I'm Joseph Joestar, an American!

138
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:20,117
I'm staying at Hotel Clark's! What?!

139
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:24,620
And by the way, girly, I have a thing
for hot, young nurses like yourself.

140
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,760
I think I should give you an exam!

141
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,030
What?!

142
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,060
Wait! It's not true!

143
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:33,780
Oh, no!

144
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:49,920
Ha ha ha!

145
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,359
Now you can't go back to the hotel!

146
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,460
You're all alone now, honey!

147
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:57,211
I can kill you without anyone interfering!

148
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:58,477
You little...

149
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,260
you're pissing me off!

150
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,720
I'll crush you to tiny bits!

151
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,680
What? Hey!

152
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,500
This is your own arm!

153
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,977
Take care of it, you shitty old man!

154
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:11,720
It grew arms.

155
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,060
How much more could it grow?

156
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,220
What the hell?

157
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,420
Let go of it!

158
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:23,180
I mean it, freak! Now!

159
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,640
Not a chance!

160
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,310
Hey, officer!

161
00:10:26,393 --> 00:10:28,320
The murderer's over here!

162
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:29,960
He's right here!

163
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:34,600
It's been a while since it's come to this.

164
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:37,220
Hey, what are you doing?

165
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:41,390
Overdrive!

166
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,330
Huh?

167
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:48,590
Moron!

168
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,880
It's your arm, remember?

169
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:55,840
You think your hamon would work against
your own body? Hands up! Don't move!

170
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:58,620
Then how about perfect purple?

171
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,437
You're crushing me!

172
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,049
I can use it this way too!

173
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,689
So how does it feel, ugly?

174
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,841
I told you not to move, now free!

175
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:17,920
Damn it! What are you
doing? I can't see! Shit!

176
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,573
Jesus, Mary and Joseph!

177
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,374
Do you get what I'm telling you, Nena?

178
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:41,297
Uh, real men don't have to talk a big
game like your six-shooting boyfriend.

179
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:45,439
That's how you figure out who's a
liar and who's the genuine article.

180
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,837
Damn cops have run me
in the wrong direction.

181
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,744
I'm nowhere near the hotel now.

182
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:56,136
If I had known this would happen, I
would have taken Polnareff with me.

183
00:11:56,400 --> 00:12:00,180
Instead of a petty guy like
Whole Horse, why not be with me?

184
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,518
Am I not your type?

185
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,520
Come on, I don't dwell
on the past like some.

186
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:10,277
I don't care who you were
dating before even Whole Horse.

187
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,184
What's important is the future.

188
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:15,017
We just need to understand
each other, right?

189
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,960
Oh, look over there, Polnareff.

190
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:21,365
That place is a hotel run by a
nice Japanese woman named Kumiko.

191
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,494
She manages it with her Indian husband.

192
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,617
We can probably get a cheap room.

193
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,540
Oh, really?

194
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,840
Tell me more about this hotel.

195
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,350
What?

196
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:50,140
What the hell are you doing?!

197
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,690
Huh?

198
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,800
Jummy Man!

199
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,360
I'm eating, Joestar!

200
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,617
A growing girl needs her food!

201
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:03,040
You stole those at the market,
you quick little bastard!

202
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:09,240
Why, you...

203
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:14,340
Choo-me-mean!

204
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,480
Look how big I've gotten! It's tough!

205
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:20,880
Having another mouse to
feed isn't it, Daddy?

206
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,160
Choo-me-mean!

207
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,400
You disgusting little cow!

208
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,697
I'll show you that nobody
has the experience or

209
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:31,662
the smarts to take down
the great Joseph Joestar.

210
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:34,115
You don't stand a chance, you bastard!

211
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:37,160
Now how the hell am I
gonna do that? Damn it!

212
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,680
Here goes nothing.

213
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:39,980
Hermit Purple!

214
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:48,780
Oh, Daddy dearest, you've done
a wonderful job of raising me.

215
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:52,897
But you know, you shouldn't tie your
children down or they won't grow.

216
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,560
Oh, it only smothers them.

217
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,980
You should raise them to be free.

218
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:58,720
If not, they might rebel!

219
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,700
Oh, no!

220
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:07,660
It's no use.

221
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:09,000
If I had a camera,

222
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:12,717
I could use Hermit Purple to get a
picture of the Stan user's location.

223
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:13,640
Damn it all!

224
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:17,040
Come on, think, Joseph, think.

225
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:20,015
At this rate, it won't just be my arm.

226
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:22,180
She'll take over my whole body.

227
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,290
Huh?

228
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:25,830
Whoa!

229
00:14:27,220 --> 00:14:28,050
Huh?

230
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:33,500
I've already grown enough that I could
easily end your pathetic life. See?

231
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:36,340
My hand can reach your
throat now, old man.

232
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,277
I just have to bust
your carotid artery and

233
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,948
you'll crumple over
like a sack of potatoes.

234
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:45,450
Whoa!

235
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,580
Oh, no!

236
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:01,940
What's he doing?

237
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:07,090
Bastard!

238
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:09,740
He's lost his mind! Look at that!

239
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:13,260
Some very strange man has a
strange growth on his arm!

240
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:16,490
Damn it!

241
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,560
Where the hell's the stand user?

242
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:26,800
I have to tell you something. Huh?

243
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,980
I need a reliable man, a good
man like you, to take care of me.

244
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,800
And I love you, Polnareff.

245
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:36,607
Such a kind-hearted,
trustworthy man you are.

246
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,110
Really?

247
00:15:38,193 --> 00:15:39,353
But it's all so sudden.

248
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,557
This is happening!

249
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,137
I have finally found one!

250
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:43,440
G-g-lucky!

251
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:21,740
Hey, Joseph Joestar, you idiot!

252
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:25,825
You keep getting farther and
farther from Jotaro and the others!

253
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:29,397
Do you really think I'm just
running around town randomly?

254
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:32,598
I'm not doing this just to
wear myself out, you know!

255
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:36,600
I'm running so I can kill you!

256
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:38,660
This is the end of the line!

257
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:40,100
See that?

258
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:42,020
You're going in!

259
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:43,660
Have a nice soap!

260
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,120
You senile old fool!

261
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,550
Yeah!

262
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,030
A nail?

263
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,040
Yeah, I picked it up earlier,

264
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:03,613
when you were rolling around
on the ground like an idiot.

265
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:09,060
Now I can shove it right in your carotid
and you'll bleed out like a stuck pig.

266
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:13,860
Did you actually believe I'd suffocate
if you stuck me in here, you fool!

267
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,530
Die!

268
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:22,200
I may be made of your flesh,
but I'm nothing like you!

269
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,480
Forget the rules already, Chunk!

270
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:29,320
Only a stand can hope to
defeat another stand! Oh, yeah!

271
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:33,617
Didn't you say you were gonna show me
all that fighting experience you have?

272
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:36,480
Was I supposed to be
impressed? So blessed!

273
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:41,646
You're just a helpless geezer who's gotten
too old to help anyone, even himself!

274
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,820
My prosthetic hand!

275
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:46,797
It was on the verge of breaking
from her attack earlier,

276
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:49,380
and now I can't get any strength into it!

277
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,140
Just one more push!

278
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:55,137
Your life as an invalid is about
to come to an end, if you be mean.

279
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:57,749
There's not a single
way you can defeat me.

280
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,720
You might as well surrender.

281
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:06,020
What the hell is this?

282
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:17,140
I might as well what now?

283
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:21,420
I'm sorry, my hearing isn't
exactly what it once was.

284
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:24,140
Run that by me one more time, will ya?

285
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,640
It's Kultar!

286
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:29,800
That was your plan all along!

287
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:34,180
It wasn't to suffocate me, you
were trying to keep me from moving!

288
00:18:34,940 --> 00:18:35,880
But how?

289
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:39,120
How did you know there
was Kultar in there?

290
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:45,000
With my sands power, Hermit
Purple told me everything!

291
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:49,360
Hey, everyone, look! What is this?

292
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:53,696
The ashes that foreigners spilled
everywhere when he wrecked the place.

293
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:57,720
They formed into a
perfect map of the city.

294
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:01,620
You drew a map with Hermit Purple?

295
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,666
That's how you found the tar?

296
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:06,360
A map out of incense ashes?

297
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:11,697
Yeah, now I think even a glorified a
pimple like you should see the difference?

298
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:13,317
in our fighting experience.

299
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:17,060
When your opponent starts
boasting, he's already lost.

300
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:20,720
That shrew is a line from my wilder days.

301
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,360
Like a fine wine, I guess
I just get better with age.

302
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:29,120
And now, a stand will
defeat another stand.

303
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:32,657
Next you'll say, please
stop it, I beg you.

304
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,860
Please just stop it, I beg you.

305
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:40,300
This will hurt me as much as it hurts you.

306
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:43,720
But children can't depend
on their parents forever.

307
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:50,080
Once you've grown up, you've got
to learn to live on your own.

308
00:19:59,020 --> 00:20:03,060
Now then, I wonder where that
thing stand user is hiding.

309
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:12,700
Ah, so, what do you say, Nena, darling?

310
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:16,960
Shall we seal our new
love with a sweet kiss?

311
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:24,440
What the hell is this? It's nasty!

312
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,500
What's wrong, Nena?

313
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,130
Ah!

314
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:42,400
So, she was the empress's
stand user all along.

315
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:46,820
She was an ugly old troll.

316
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,537
She attached her stand to
me as a tumor with a human

317
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,680
face and camouflaged herself
as a beautiful woman.

318
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,180
You were careless.

319
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:57,320
She played you like a
damn fiddle, Polnareff.

320
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,280
Oh, oh!

321
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:21,177
And here I thought we'd finally be
able to sleep in a bed for once.

322
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:25,317
If the old man hadn't screwed up, he
wouldn't be out here hiding from the cops.

323
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,780
I took care of things.

324
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,877
We can take this car.

325
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,760
Polnareff, you do the driving.

326
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:33,950
What?

327
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:36,098
Don't tell me you're still in shock.

328
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:39,060
I was the one who was
attacked by the stand.

329
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:42,539
Sure, but I think I'd rather
have gone through that.

330
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:14,977
All the old paintings on the tomb.

331
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:17,017
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

332
00:22:17,100 --> 00:22:19,257
If you move too quick, oh well!

333
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:21,697
They're falling down like a domino.

334
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:24,377
All the buzzer men by the Nile.

335
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:27,997
They got their money on
a bed Called crocodiles.

336
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:28,937
Oh-eh-oh.

337
00:22:29,020 --> 00:22:30,937
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

338
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:33,177
Fallen types of the hookah. I say.

339
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:40,917
Oh-eh-oh.

340
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,294
Walk like an Egyptian.

341
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,597
The blonde waitresses.

342
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:58,977
Take their trays, spin around
and they cross the floor.

343
00:22:59,060 --> 00:23:01,677
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more.

344
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,317
All the school kids so sick of books.

345
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:06,357
They're like the punk and the metal band.

346
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:10,617
When the buzzer rings, they're
walking like an Egyptian.

347
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:13,277
All the kids in the marketplace say.

348
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:14,257
Walk

349
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:21,340
like

350
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:22,270
an Egyptian?

351
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:28,177
I guess it's time to say goodbye to India.

352
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:29,907
I mean, come on, I'm a girl.

353
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:32,377
So, did you get a look
at the driver's face?

354
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:34,817
I'm saying we don't need
any more trouble now.

355
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:36,253
Where'd that come from?

356
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:37,931
I got a question for you.

357
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:39,300
You like sumo?
